Patches applied to the deps/libdb submodule before building it.

Named libdb-<pinned tag>-<topic>.patch, applied with "cd deps/libdb &&
patch -p1" idempotently by deps/build_libdb.sh.  Drop a patch when the
pin moves past the upstream commit that carries the same fix.

## Current patches (pin v2026.10.7 = a849cdbc5)

None.

The four libdb fixes dbsql carried against v2026.10.5 (R7, R9, R10, R11)
are upstream as of libdb v2026.10.6 (commits 0379bd0c9, 7f04b0de3,
71fb9d711, c107ddd09), so the source patches were dropped when the pin
moved to v2026.10.7.  The upstream R10 fix is broader than the one dbsql
carried: it also stops __env_attach_regions from panicking on a
transient EMFILE while bringing the regions up (src/env/env_open.c), the
second EMFILE site that dbsql had left unfixed (SQLite misc7).

The reproducers, regression tests and the full git-format-patch set are
kept in .agent/libdb-bugs/ for the record and for re-filing if a future
pin ever regresses them.  See .agent/libdb-bugs/README.md.

## History

The libtool FreeBSD host-pattern fix this directory carried for
v2026.10.1/.2 (freebsd1* matching FreeBSD 10-19, so no shared library
was built) is upstream as of libdb v2026.10.3 (6e1f1c86a).

Note: in v2026.10.3+ five build_windows/*.sln/*.vcproj files are stored
with CRLF line endings against .gitattributes' "* text=auto", so
"git status" in the submodule lists them as modified on a fresh
checkout.  Cosmetic; the build does not use them.
